**Input Data**

Five-granularity linguistic term set:

\[
S=\{s_{-2},s_{-1},s_{0},s_{1},s_{2}\},\qquad \tau=2
\]

Standard utility function:

\[
g(s_a)=\frac{a+2}{4}
\]

Thus,

\[
g(s_0)=0.50,\qquad g(s_1)=0.75
\]

Two benchmark cases are used: \(x_1\) (low-end screen) and \(x_2\) (high-end screen). The system-standard utilities are:

\[
\nu_s=(\nu_s(x_1),\nu_s(x_2))=(0.30,\ 0.70)
\]

The experts’ subjective utilities for the two benchmark cases are:

| Expert | Type | \(\nu_p(x_1)\) | \(\nu_p(x_2)\) |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| \(E_1\) | Strict / pessimistic, overall lower | 0.25 | 0.65 |
| \(E_2\) | Lenient / optimistic, overall higher | 0.35 | 0.75 |
| \(E_3\) | Neutral | 0.30 | 0.70 |

**Computation of \(\alpha\) and \(\beta\) Using Eqs. (4) and (5)**

\[
\alpha_k=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\frac{\nu_s(x_i)}{\nu_p(x_i)},
\qquad
\beta_k=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left(\nu_s(x_i)-\nu_p(x_i)\right),
\]

where \(m=2\).

For \(E_1\):

\[
\alpha_1=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{0.30}{0.25}+\frac{0.70}{0.65}\right)
=\frac{1}{2}(1.2000+1.0769)=1.1385
\]

\[
\beta_1=\frac{1}{2}\left[(0.30-0.25)+(0.70-0.65)\right]
=\frac{1}{2}(0.05+0.05)=0.05
\]

For \(E_2\):

\[
\alpha_2=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{0.30}{0.35}+\frac{0.70}{0.75}\right)
=\frac{1}{2}(0.8571+0.9333)=0.8952
\]

\[
\beta_2=\frac{1}{2}\left[(0.30-0.35)+(0.70-0.75)\right]
=\frac{1}{2}(-0.05-0.05)=-0.05
\]

For \(E_3\):

\[
\alpha_3=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{0.30}{0.30}+\frac{0.70}{0.70}\right)=1.0000
\]

\[
\beta_3=\frac{1}{2}\left[(0.30-0.30)+(0.70-0.70)\right]=0
\]

The resulting calibration parameters are:

| Expert | \(\alpha_k\) | \(\beta_k\) | Calibration function \(f_k(x)=\alpha_k x+\beta_k\) |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| \(E_1\) | 1.1385 | 0.05 | \(f_1(x)=1.1385x+0.05\) |
| \(E_2\) | 0.8952 | \(-0.05\) | \(f_2(x)=0.8952x-0.05\) |
| \(E_3\) | 1.0000 | 0 | \(f_3(x)=x\) |
